TypeScript adaptation adds finite planned sample metadata, asynchronous bounded
WriteHandle writes, input packet validation, cancellation and output abort.

CLI stream selection adapts pinned fftools/ffmpeg_mux_init.c (map_auto_video,
map_auto_audio and disposition propagation), LGPL-2.1-or-later, plus MOV enabled
track handling from movenc.c. These files are part of FFmpeg; their upstream
notices and source remain in the pinned submodule. AAC configuration parsing
supplies codec channel counts for selection; no decoder runs in the library.

Language conversion/table adapts pinned libavformat/isom.c:
Copyright (c)2001 Fabrice Bellard; (c)2002 Francois Revol;
(c)2006 Baptiste Coudurier. LGPL-2.1-or-later.
Mux invalid-language normalization follows movenc.c (32767 sentinel).

Edited video copy duration tracking follows movenc.c end_pts/elst_end_pts.
Strict mux DTS correction follows fftools/ffmpeg_mux.c at the same commit.
The adaptation keeps original packet timestamps for input-plan validation and
records destination sample deltas separately for STTS serialization.

Zero-packet nonfragmented output omits empty trak boxes, following
mov_write_moov_tag, and computes next_track_ID from nonempty track IDs as in
mov_write_mvhd_tag. Planned stream indices remain intact for packet validation.

AAC presentation/end-edit tracking follows movenc.c handling of
AV_PKT_DATA_SKIP_SAMPLES: effective presentation duration is the larger of
nominal codec-frame duration and packet duration, less discard padding. STTS
keeps its planned packet durations. Source skip-sample stamps are deep-copied
and validated during payload consumption; changes abort without commit.

AAC output-clock conversion and stateful coarse timestamp correction in
src/mp4/aac-copy-clock.ts/copy-plan.ts adapt av_rescale_delta from pinned
libavutil/mathematics.c and mux_fixup_ts from fftools/ffmpeg_mux.c, under
LGPL-2.1-or-later. Original copyright notices and license text remain in the
pinned upstream submodule. mov_init movie-timescale selection uses original
input clocks before audio track clocks become sample-rate clocks. The source
clock/duration plan markers are separately checked against payload iteration.

AAC copy sample-entry rate/channel regeneration follows pinned
libavformat/movenc.c mov_write_audio_tag: codec channel count and sample rate,
with rate shifted until representable in the16-bit word for MP4 entries.
Encoded payload and AudioSpecificConfig bytes are retained.

AAC copy rate resolution uses effective demux codec parameters after MOV's
zero-rate fallback;unresolved sample rates fail before output publication.
Native/Core exact exit-code mapping remains a documented known difference.
